{"parentUuid":"582ac325-7ace-4850-808f-18e838fdc950","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpPv6FaVJKL1sQySUEyh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_read_input_tokens":568044,"output_tokens":1148,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":183},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":568044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8736,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e1037b42-236b-415d-999e-dfbb15a71d1c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpPv5j5WJA8sNwPdpFHM","requestRef":"13341ccd-1ad8-4a09-89e2-097c3495728b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f259933-07a3-40e3-b1c8-d05a6e079b47","timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:58:28.776Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"0f259933-07a3-40e3-b1c8-d05a6e079b47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpPv6FaVJKL1sQySUEyh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both pages are rebuilt in Callio Labs' style, and the neuron is now movable with no flash. The production build passes, and I checked the landing page and dashboard in screenshots.\n\n**Movable and no flash.** The neuron works like Callio's DNA viewer: it slowly auto-rotates, and you can drag it to spin it. Zoom is off, as in Callio. The firing effects are gone completely: no pulse, flash, ripple or grey-to-colour shift. The drag now uses three.js's standard OrbitControls, so the drag I tested earlier no longer applies. I've only confirmed the auto-rotation, so give the drag a quick try.\n\n**Landing page (`/`)**\n- The neuron is translucent grey, auto-rotating, and runs diagonally across the page.\n- Behind it is Callio's black-and-white dither background, which reacts to the mouse.\n- The wordmark \"motus\" is in Chillax with \"early ALS detection\" in Synonym, plus Callio's glass \"Sign in with Google\" pill.\n- Callio's white loading splash fades out once the model has loaded.\n- The model's CC BY credit stays at the bottom right.\n\n**Dashboard (`/home`)**\n- Callio's light, black-and-white look, on the same dither background.\n- Inset sidebar, top to bottom: the \"motus\" wordmark, a dark \"New assessment\" button, your main pages, labelled Assessments and Clinical groups, then Devices & capture, Data & privacy and Settings, with your account menu at the bottom.\n- A thin header with the sidebar toggle and the page title.\n- All the existing dashboard content is still there, on frosted cards with Callio's blue chart colours. I added a frosted panel behind \"Welcome back\" so it reads over the dither.\n\n**Worth knowing**\n- **Performance:** the dither background is a heavy shader. In my headless test it nearly froze rendering, but that was a software GPU. Check it feels smooth on the expo laptop. If it doesn't, turning off its mouse interaction or using a larger pixel size will help.\n- **Fonts:** I copied Chillax and Synonym from your Callio repo. Chillax's free-use licence is saved in `public/fonts/chillax/LICENSE.txt`. Synonym had no licence file in Callio, so I couldn't copy one.\n- **Replaced code:** the old firing simulation, generated neuron and grain background are now unused. I moved those files to a backup folder rather than deleting them, since none of this has been committed yet:\n  - `C:\\Users\\jerem\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\2ea77955cf64b3d5\\28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab\\scratchpad\\motus-backup`\n\n  I also removed the packages they used.\n- **Copied over:** `Dither` and `GlassSurface` came across unchanged into `src/components/react-bits/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_read_input_tokens":568044,"output_tokens":1148,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":183},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":568044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e1037b42-236b-415d-999e-dfbb15a71d1c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgpPv5j5WJA8sNwPdpFHM","requestRef":"13341ccd-1ad8-4a09-89e2-097c3495728b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4b34ade5-f8a7-47e3-bdbc-b875f3abee24","timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:58:31.385Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5"