{"parentUuid":"aeec3af4-1ca1-4612-a138-0a7a1c775025","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpQZZL2U8FSnieuEhrYX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've done all three: the loading screen is gone, the neuron stands upright and spins about its vertical axis, and both pages now have their own identity rather than copying Callio. The production build passes, and I checked the landing page and dashboard in screenshots.\n\n**The neuron**\n- **Upright:** turned 90°, with dendrites and cell body at the top and the axon running down to its terminals.\n- **Spin:** it slowly turns about that vertical axis. Dragging only turns it left and right, and it can't tip over or zoom.\n- **Placement:** no diagonal tilt any more; it stands in the right part of the screen, clear of the title.\n\n**No loading screen.** The model is 288 KB, so it just fades in over about 0.7 s once loaded. The splash is removed from both the landing page and the dashboard.\n\n**Motus' own identity**\n| | Callio | Motus now |\n|---|---|---|\n| Colour | Pure black and white | Warm paper (#f6f3ed) with ink-navy (#13293d) dither, and a teal-ink neuron |\n| Wordmark | Chillax | Sora, Motus' original font |\n| Subtitle | Synonym serif | Instrument Serif italic: \"early ALS detection, from how you move\" |\n| Sign-in | Glass pill | Solid ink pill with a white circle around the colour Google \"G\" |\n| Dashboard | Black-and-white tokens, blue charts | Same paper, ink and teal palette, with teal-to-navy charts and the Sora wordmark in the sidebar |\n\nWhat's still shared with Callio: the dither background behind both pages and the inset-sidebar dashboard layout.\n\n**Removed:** Callio's splash, its glass button, and the copied Chillax and Synonym font files (along with their licence file), since nothing uses them now. The palette lives in `src/index.css`, plus `src/lib/theme.ts` for the two background colours, so retuning it is quick."}],"container