{"parentUuid":"2fee3912-e0f3-4791-aa65-e3cdbaddc7e7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_013siaBrKeM7mr62cz4co3Ag","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c7ac73b9-d276-4c65-9cff-0a0d1ab27e95","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:20:03.316Z","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"c7ac73b9-d276-4c65-9cff-0a0d1ab27e95","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpRZmBnWHCWbHeA1fGYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The neuron now fires and is slanted. The build passes, and I checked a sequence of frames from one full firing.\n\n**Firing.** It fires every 2.6 to 3.8 seconds, in four steps:\n1. **Inputs:** a soft band slides inward along the dendrites toward the cell body.\n2. **Cell body:** it briefly deepens in colour.\n3. **Action potential:** a deep-teal band runs down the axon and through the myelin segments.\n4. **Release:** as the band reaches each terminal, it releases a small puff of teal particles. These are very faint; you'll probably barely notice them.\n\nThe signal is shown as the membrane going darker and more saturated, not lighting up, so it fits the paper-and-ink style. My first try made the cell body too bright a cyan; I darkened the pulse colour and toned the cell-body step down. It's off for visitors with reduced motion turned on.\n\n**Slant.** The whole frame is tilted, so the neuron still spins cleanly about its own length rather than wobbling. The model already had a slight lean of its own, and my first 14° tilt cancelled it out so it looked straight. I flipped the direction: it now runs from the cell body at top-left down to the terminals at bottom-right. I also shrank it a little, since the tilted frame was clipping it at the top and bottom.\n\nTo adjust, the settings are at the top of `src/components/neuron-viewer.tsx`:\n- `SLANT_DEG`: the tilt;\n- `PULSE`: the firing colour;\n- `INPUT_S` and `AP_SPEED`: firing timing;\n- `BURST`: particles per terminal.\n\nThe firing interval itself is set in the firing loop further down that file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":576,"cache_read_input_tokens":630538,"output_tokens":562,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":576,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":630538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":576},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"90145843-c3d2-48a6-ba3d-8fa3189b6bca","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpRZkjW8M42nA4amCMhY","requestRef":"d45aa0da-3aef-45e1-b739-5dcc75289539","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"64dbf868-380c-413e-b313-6a9d3e2922fa","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:20:03.315Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
