{"parentUuid":"355e3088-34b9-4a16-8fdd-54ef54b59b97","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpT9CJvG4pq4oCWhENS9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, it's not Next.js. It's a **Vite + React 19 + TypeScript** single-page app, using react-router-dom for the `/` and `/home` routes, plus Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui, and React Three Fiber for the 3D. It runs with `npm run dev` and builds to a static `dist/` folder.\n\nBoth reference projects are Next.js: Callio Labs uses Next 15 and calhacks uses Next 16. I kept Vite because `frontend/` started empty and card.io (also Vite) was the first reference. Vite also matches the stack in this repo's `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nIf you want it in Next, moving it is fairly mechanical:\n- **Pages:** `pages/Landing.tsx` and `pages/Home.tsx` become `app/page.tsx` and `app/home/page.tsx`.\n- **3D and background components:** they need `\"use client\"` and loading with `dynamic(..., { ssr: false })`, the way Callio does it.\n- **Environment variables:** `VITE_SUPABASE_*` becomes `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*`.\n- **Sign-in:** this is the main design choice. Keep today's browser-only Supabase sign-in (simplest), or switch to `@supabase/ssr` with a `/auth/callback` route and cookie sessions like calhacks. The second lets the server check sessions before rendering `/home`.\n\nIt's worth switching if you'll want server-side routes, such as API endpoints for the typing, speech and handwriting data, or if your team's other projects are all Next. For a static landing page and dashboard on sample data, Vite is fine. Should I move it?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7,"cache_read_input_tokens":632107,"output_tokens":649,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":90},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":632107,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"39e32d5f-964d-4ced-883b-6631f34a9478","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgpT8h7VQ29MmyXgM1XCi","requestRef":"2a620988-20a4-4ec4-bf11-e2402bf1a1e5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"240198b0-b6da-485f-8430-e53c863fb8eb","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:40:44.781Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
