{"parentUuid":"96e1f64d-b651-4702-a894-b410e545f7af","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_015dNAbTAzhCSgUnTQhs1GBq","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6f6d809b-df96-41de-9a8d-d3a649d77a75","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:53:30.626Z","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"6f6d809b-df96-41de-9a8d-d3a649d77a75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpU7jKHx4ef7N8pZQg6s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've reworked the firing so it's a warm amber spark instead of the muddy dark teal. The build passes, and I checked a sequence of frames from one firing, apart from my last small tweak (see below).\n\nThe old pulse was a darker teal on a teal cell, and the lighting greyed it further, so it read as a smudge rather than a signal. Now:\n\n- **Colour:** the signal is amber (`#f2852f`), the complement of the teal membrane, so it stands out against the paper background. It's drawn so the 3D lighting doesn't grey it out.\n- **Axon pulse:** a crisp, narrow amber band runs down through the myelin segments, with a short fading tail behind it so you can see which way it's travelling.\n- **Cell body:** a soft amber glow kept to the cell body. My first version washed peach over the body and half the dendrites, which read as a flash again.\n- **Incoming signals:** a faint ring closing in on the cell body, toned well down.\n- **Terminals:** the branch tips light up amber as the pulse arrives, and release amber particles that are now slightly larger so they actually show.\n\nI haven't screenshotted the final trim to the incoming ring. Watch the moment the cell body fires: if it still spills onto the dendrites, it's a one-number change.\n\nEverything is in `src/components/neuron-viewer.tsx`:\n- **`PULSE`** sets the colour.\n- **`pulseK = clamp(...)`** weighs each part (axon wave, incoming ring, cell body).\n- **`* 0.75` in `pulseEmissive`** sets how strongly it glows."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_read_input_tokens":655165,"output_tokens":528,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":655165,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d236158b-f3f7-4686-a6eb-7dc42ba3b336","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpU7ihLJtwSgKd7Mr3hb","requestRef":"bfac48d7-c187-467a-8dd2-d3af60ef01fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f633cc33-453b-4d9e-b70f-ad7cc8e54455","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:53:30.624Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
