{"parentUuid":"d6cec748-b36f-4669-9c20-022b198a978f","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"You're building the Addo Labs landing page and dashboard; it's now renamed, with neuron icons and an amber firing neuron. Next: tell me what the dashboard should show, since it still tracks patient symptoms rather than drug discovery.","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:19:46.716Z","uuid":"9d742922-37a9-4ea2-adf9-17bf734ca495","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"9d742922-37a9-4ea2-adf9-17bf734ca495","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fa5473ad-dd00-4735-b27d-2f32ee1ccee6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Here's the current idea and workflow we're going with for the idea: \n\n<pasted_content id=\"f540\">\nPitch: BBB was the biggest barrier to drug delivery for ALS. With Focus MRI from Sunnybrook, we can now look into new drugs that couldn't penetrate the BBB that can potentially reduce symptoms, develop a cure, or increase life expectancy. \n\nPipeline: \nAI agent analyzes patient data with tools calls to NCBI and other drug datasets, develops a characteristic of the ideal drug\nRun this agent in parallel 5 times, with each agent producing a slightly different drug profile\nRun each profile against an embedding model, the same one used in the DRKG database\nA research agent that has open search enabled will then analyze the top drugs that relate to each embedding using cosine similarity and ranks each drug with analysis of effects, symtoms, etc based on the user\nOutput a report with citations and clear description of each drug and the new potential it provides as an alternative therapeutic approach\n\nThings to consider:\ncost of the drug/treatment\navailability (if it exists in the country or not) + regulations\nuser acceptance (if the user would consent to it, how popular/standardized the drug is)\nsafety/side effects to other conditions/exsiting medication\n</pasted_content id=\"f540\">\n\n\nThis is a very similar workflow to callio labs. Refer to the github repo for callio labs and build something similar in terms of workflow but also that has it's own touch in ALS and neurology"},"uuid":"fd87a2ae-3e68-4d80-bb60-480096deedf3","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:22:21.374Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":20,"turnIndex":27},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend