{"parentUuid":"6e81e0e9-def4-49eb-9f21-86e0ab4480da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpksVJmEHeUJGqNe3oEz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":646510,"output_tokens":1506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":646510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8537,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"02d5b27b-4bfe-4c27-be0d-c9f9a3a1a5da","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpksUzAJanDCLqpHJzQu","requestRef":"77b5a0b4-0be9-46be-b397-dc09cc4d9324","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"924150fd-f5c1-4b4b-89c5-509876599c11","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:33:17.181Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"924150fd-f5c1-4b4b-89c5-509876599c11","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpksVJmEHeUJGqNe3oEz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard now runs your discovery pipeline, laid out like Callio's agent workflow, from the patient record through the five profile agents, DRKG matching and a research agent to a cited report. The build passes and I clicked through a full run in screenshots. The run itself is scripted, the same way Callio's demo was, so no real agents, searches or embeddings happen yet.\n\n**How a run plays out (Discovery page)**\n1. **Set up:** you see the patient card (ALSFRS-R slope, genetics, current meds, comorbidities, location and coverage, preferences, and an \"MRgFUS eligible\" badge). Next to it is an editable research goal and on/off switches for your four considerations plus mechanistic fit, then \"Run 5 agents\".\n2. **Progress rail:** five stages across the top. The profile-agents stage has five coloured bars that fill in as each agent finishes.\n3. **Agent trace:** Callio-style collapsible rows for thinking, tool calls (NCBI, ClinVar, Open Targets, DRKG, web search, interaction check) and results, grouped by stage. The five agents' steps interleave, each with its lane colour.\n4. **Result tabs** that open as each stage finishes:\n   - **Profiles:** five ideal-drug profiles (neurotrophic, cytokine neuroinflammation, complement, TDP-43 proteostasis, excitotoxicity), each with targets, modality and constraints.\n   - **Embedding:** a 2D map of the DRKG embedding space with each profile's vector and its nearest drugs, plus the cosine scores.\n   - **Candidates:** ranked table with fit, safety, cost, access and acceptance scores, and BBB penetrance alone versus with MRgFUS. Toggling a consideration re-ranks it live. An \"Excluded for this patient\" list follows (e.g. tofersen because the patient is SOD1-negative; riluzole and edaravone because they're already prescribed).\n   - **Report:** summary, patient context, method, ranked candidates with cost, availability, acceptance, safety and evidence, exclusions, limitations and numbered references. \"Save as PDF\" prints only the report.\n5. **Skip to results** jumps straight to the end, useful at the expo table.\n\n**Other pages**\n- **Runs & reports:** each finished run as a paper preview, like Callio's Projects; click to reopen its report.\n- **Patient overview:** the earlier motor-function dashboard, reframed as patient data the agents read.\n- **Sidebar:** reorganised into Discovery, Patient data and Delivery & access groups. The new pages are placeholders.\n\n**Before you demo this**\n- **Illustrative content.** The candidates, scores, availability and cost notes are mine, written to be plausible. I kept the drug facts to ones I'm fairly confident of, such as mechanisms, the meningococcal warning on ravulizumab, and tocilizumab's effect on the enzyme that clears riluzole. A teammate with clinical knowledge should still check them. The UI labels everything \"Simulated run · illustrative outputs\".\n- **Citations.** I only cited seven papers I'm confident are real, including Abrahao 2019 (the Sunnybrook focused-ultrasound ALS trial), DRKG, and the riluzole, edaravone and tofersen trials. Each links to a PubMed search, not a DOI, so a misremembered DOI can't send judges to the wrong paper.\n- **Connecting real agents.** The whole run goes through one function, `runDemoPipeline` in `src/lib/pipeline.ts`. A real backend only needs to send the same events (stage started or finished, trace step, profile ready, results ready). Because this is a static Vite app, the agents would have to live somewhere else, for example a small Python service, which also suits the DRKG embeddings.\n\nNew code is in `src/components/discovery/` (`workspace.tsx`, `report.tsx`, `runs.tsx`) and `src/lib/pipeline.ts`. Nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":646510,"output_tokens":1506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":646510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"02d5b27b-4bfe-4c27-be0d-c9f9a3a1a5da","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgpksUzAJanDCLqpHJzQu","requestRef":"77b5a0b4-0be9-46be-b397-dc09cc4d9324","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"281e3630-f68b-40b4-995a-e49a2823e40d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:33:23.354Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
