84-979ba4420a6f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"context7","attributionMcpTool":"resolve-library-id","type":"assistant","uuid":"c043f981-8f8c-412e-bbc5-4ca983e57e96","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:45:30.190Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"b28574d1-1efc-42c5-a0dc-6323cc7b72b6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23fb2881-f29f-424e-b551-8c71406ef78f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TMHdxRNiMo76tsT54Num2H","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Extract text content from page\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/PDFPageProxy.md\n\nExample of extracting text from a page using getTextContent with includeMarkedContent. Filters items that have a 'str' property and joins them with spaces.\n\n```javascript\nconst textContent = await page.getTextContent({ includeMarkedContent: true });\nconst text = textContent.items\n  .filter((item) => \"str\" in item)\n  .map((item) => item.str)\n  .join(\" \");\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### cleanup and _destroy > Example — text extraction\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/PDFPageProxy.md\n\n### Example — text extraction\n\n```js\nconst textContent = await page.getTextContent({ includeMarkedContent: true });\nconst text = textContent.items\n  .filter((item) => \"str\" in item)\n  .map((item) => item.str)\n  .join(\" \");\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### getDocument(src)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/getDocument.md\n\nLoads a PDF document from a URL, binary data, or parameter object and returns a PDFDocumentLoadingTask whose promise resolves to a PDFDocumentProxy. This is the main entry point for the pdfjs-dist library.\n\n```APIDOC\n## getDocument(src)\n\n### Description\nLoads a PDF document and returns a loading task whose `promise` resolves to a `PDFDocumentProxy`. This is the main entry point for the whole library.\n\n### Method\nFunction call\n\n### Signature\n```ts\nexport function getDocument(src: GetDocumentParameters): PDFDocumentLoadingTask;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n#### src (GetDocumentParameters) - Required\n- Type: `string | URL | TypedArray | ArrayBuffer | PDFDataRangeTransport | DocumentInitParameters`\n- Description: The source of the PDF document. Can be a URL string, URL object, binary data (TypedArray or ArrayBuffer), a custom range transport, or a parameter object.\n\n### Behavior\n- `string` / `URL` — the URL of the PDF; fetched with the Fetch API (XHR fallback), so same-origin/CORS rules apply.\n- `TypedArray` / `ArrayBuffer` — binary PDF data; `Uint8Array` input is used as-is; `ArrayBuffer` is wrapped; plain `Array<number>` or binary `string` input is also accepted via `data`.\n- `PDFDataRangeTransport` — custom range-request transport.\n- `DocumentInitParameters` — full options object.\n\n`src` must be a string, URL, typed array, or parameter object containing at least one of `url`, `data`, or `range`; otherwise `getDocument` throws the generic errors below.\n\n### Errors Thrown Synchronously\n| Condition | Thrown error |\n|---|---|\n| `src` is not string/URL/typed array/param object | `Error(\"Invalid parameter in getDocument, need either string, URL, TypedArray, or parameter object.\")` |\n| param object has none of `.data`, `.range`, `.url` | `Error(\"Invalid parameter object: need either .data, .range or .url\")` |\n| `url` is not a string/URL object | `Error(\"Invalid PDF url data: either string or URL-object is expected in the url property.\")` |\n| `data` is not TypedArray, string, array-like, or ArrayBuffer | `Error(\"Invalid PDF binary data: either TypedArray, string, or array-like object is expected in the data property.\")` |\n\n### Defaults Applied Inside `getDocument`\n- `params.CMapReaderFactory = params.CMapReaderFactory || DefaultCMapReaderFactory` (`DOMCMapReaderFactory`)\n- `params.StandardFontDataFactory = params.StandardFontDataFactory || DefaultStandardFontDataFactory` (`DOMStandardFontDataFactory`)\n- `params.ignoreErrors = params.stopAtErrors !== true`\n- `rangeChunkSize` defaults to `DEFAULT_RANGE_CHUNK_SIZE` (65536) when not a positive integer\n- `maxImageSize` defaults to `-1`; `docBaseUrl` to `null`; `cMapUrl`/`standardFontDataUrl` to `null`\n- `useWorkerFetch`, `isEvalSupported` (`true`), `isOffscreenCanvasSupported` (`!isNodeJS`), `disableFontFace` (`isNodeJS`), `useSystemFonts` (`!isNodeJS && !disableFontFace`), `ownerDocument` (`globalThis.document`), `disableRange`/`disableStream`/`disableAutoFetch` (`false`)\n- If `src` is a `PDFDataRangeTransport`, `data` and `url` are ignored; the transport supplies the bytes.\n\n### Return Value\nReturns a `PDFDocumentLoadingTask` object. The `promise` property resolves to a `PDFDocumentProxy`.\n\n### Example — basic load\n```js\nimport { getDocument, GlobalWorkerOptions } from \"pdfjs-dist\";\n\nGlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = \"/pdfjs/build/pdf.worker.js\";\n\nconst loadingTask = getDocument({ url: \"https://example.com/doc.pdf\" });\nloadingTask.onProgress = ({ loaded, total }) =>\n  console.log(`Loading ${loaded} of ${total} bytes`);\n\nconst pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\nconsole.log(`Document has ${pdf.numPages} pages`);\n```\n\n### Example — binary data + error handling\n```js\nimport { getDocument, PasswordResponses } from \"pdfjs-dist\";\n\nconst response = await fetch(\"/doc.pdf\");\nconst data = new Uint8Array(await response.arrayBuffer());\n\nconst loadingTask = getDocument({ data });\n\n// Request a password when the document is encrypted.\nloadingTask.onPassword = REDACTED, reason) => {\n  if (reason === PasswordResponses.NEED_PASSWORD) {\n    updatePassword(prompt(\"Enter PDF password:\"));\n  } else if (reason === PasswordResponses.INCORRECT_PASSWORD) {\n    updatePassword(prompt(\"Incorrect password, try again:\"));\n  }\n};\n\ntry {\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  await pdf.destroy();\n} catch (reason) {\n  console.error(\"Load failed:\", reason?.name, reason?.message);\n}\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Worker URL resolution for bundlers (Vite/Webpack)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/webpack.js\n\nShows the recommended pattern for configuring PDF.js worker in bundlers like Vite or Webpack, using `new URL(..., import.meta.url)` to resolve the worker script path relative to the current module.\n\n```javascript\nconst pdfjs = require(\"./build/pdf.js\");\n\nif (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"Worker\" in window) {\n  pdfjs.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerPort = new Worker(\n    new URL(\"./build/pdf.worker.js\", import.meta.url)\n  );\n}\n\nmodule.exports = pdfjs;\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### GetDocumentParameters type alias (TypeScript)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/getDocument.md\n\nType alias for the parameter accepted by getDocument. It can be a string, URL, TypedArray, ArrayBuffer, PDFDataRangeTransport, or DocumentInitParameters.\n\n```typescript\nexport type GetDocumentParameters =\n  | string | URL | TypedArray | ArrayBuffer\n  | PDFDataRangeTransport\n  | DocumentInitParameters;\n```"}]}]},"uuid":"29a68f4a-5b38-4c8c-a419-0182dde70c7a","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:45:33.793Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### Extract text content from page\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/PDFPageProxy.md\n\nExample of extracting text from a page using getTextContent with includeMarkedContent. Filters items that have a 'str' property and joins them with spaces.\n\n```javascript\nconst textContent = await page.getTextContent({ includeMarkedContent: true });\nconst text = textContent.items\n  .filter((item) => \"str\" in item)\n  .map((item) => item.str)\n  .join(\" \");\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### cleanup and _destroy > Example — text extraction\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/PDFPageProxy.md\n\n### Example — text extraction\n\n```js\nconst textContent = await page.getTextContent({ includeMarkedContent: true });\nconst text = textContent.items\n  .filter((item) => \"str\" in item)\n  .map((item) => item.str)\n  .join(\" \");\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### getDocument(src)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/getDocument.md\n\nLoads a PDF document from a URL, binary data, or parameter object and returns a PDFDocumentLoadingTask whose promise resolves to a PDFDocumentProxy. This is the main entry point for the pdfjs-dist library.\n\n```APIDOC\n## getDocument(src)\n\n### Description\nLoads a PDF document and returns a loading task whose `promise` resolves to a `PDFDocumentProxy`. This is the main entry point for the whole library.\n\n### Method\nFunction call\n\n### Signature\n```ts\nexport function getDocument(src: GetDocumentParameters): PDFDocumentLoadingTask;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n#### src (GetDocumentParameters) - Required\n- Type: `string | URL | TypedArray | ArrayBuffer | PDFDataRangeTransport | DocumentInitParameters`\n- Description: The source of the PDF document. Can be a URL string, URL object, binary data (TypedArray or ArrayBuffer), a custom range transport, or a parameter object.\n\n### Behavior\n- `string` / `URL` — the URL of the PDF; fetched with the Fetch API (XHR fallback), so same-origin/CORS rules apply.\n- `TypedArray` / `ArrayBuffer` — binary PDF data; `Uint8Array` input is used as-is; `ArrayBuffer` is wrapped; plain `Array<number>` or binary `string` input is also accepted via `data`.\n- `PDFDataRangeTransport` — custom range-request transport.\n- `DocumentInitParameters` — full options object.\n\n`src` must be a string, URL, typed array, or parameter object containing at least one of `url`, `data`, or `range`; otherwise `getDocument` throws the generic errors below.\n\n### Errors Thrown Synchronously\n| Condition | Thrown error |\n|---|---|\n| `src` is not string/URL/typed array/param object | `Error(\"Invalid parameter in getDocument, need either string, URL, TypedArray, or parameter object.\")` |\n| param object has none of `.data`, `.range`, `.url` | `Error(\"Invalid parameter object: need either .data, .range or .url\")` |\n| `url` is not a string/URL object | `Error(\"Invalid PDF url data: either string or URL-object is expected in the url property.\")` |\n| `data` is not TypedArray, string, array-like, or ArrayBuffer | `Error(\"Invalid PDF binary data: either TypedArray, string, or array-like object is expected in the data property.\")` |\n\n### Defaults Applied Inside `getDocument`\n- `params.CMapReaderFactory = params.CMapReaderFactory || DefaultCMapReaderFactory` (`DOMCMapReaderFactory`)\n- `params.StandardFontDataFactory = params.StandardFontDataFactory || DefaultStandardFontDataFactory` (`DOMStandardFontDataFactory`)\n- `params.ignoreErrors = params.stopAtErrors !== true`\n- `rangeChunkSize` defaults to `DEFAULT_RANGE_CHUNK_SIZE` (65536) when not a positive integer\n- `maxImageSize` defaults to `-1`; `docBaseUrl` to `null`; `cMapUrl`/`standardFontDataUrl` to `null`\n- `useWorkerFetch`, `isEvalSupported` (`true`), `isOffscreenCanvasSupported` (`!isNodeJS`), `disableFontFace` (`isNodeJS`), `useSystemFonts` (`!isNodeJS && !disableFontFace`), `ownerDocument` (`globalThis.document`), `disableRange`/`disableStream`/`disableAutoFetch` (`false`)\n- If `src` is a `PDFDataRangeTransport`, `data` and `url` are ignored; the transport supplies the bytes.\n\n### Return Value\nReturns a `PDFDocumentLoadingTask` object. The `promise` property resolves to a `PDFDocumentProxy`.\n\n### Example — basic load\n```js\nimport { getDocument, GlobalWorkerOptions } from \"pdfjs-dist\";\n\nGlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = \"/pdfjs/build/pdf.worker.js\";\n\nconst loadingTask = getDocument({ url: \"https://example.com/doc.pdf\" });\nloadingTask.onProgress = ({ loaded, total }) =>\n  console.log(`Loading ${loaded} of ${total} bytes`);\n\nconst pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\nconsole.log(`Document has ${pdf.numPages} pages`);\n```\n\n### Example — binary data + error handling\n```js\nimport { getDocument, PasswordResponses } from \"pdfjs-dist\";\n\nconst response = await fetch(\"/doc.pdf\");\nconst data = new Uint8Array(await response.arrayBuffer());\n\nconst loadingTask = getDocument({ data });\n\n// Request a password when the document is encrypted.\nloadingTask.onPassword = REDACTED, reason) => {\n  if (reason === PasswordResponses.NEED_PASSWORD) {\n    updatePassword(prompt(\"Enter PDF password:\"));\n  } else if (reason === PasswordResponses.INCORRECT_PASSWORD) {\n    updatePassword(prompt(\"Incorrect password, try again:\"));\n  }\n};\n\ntry {\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  await pdf.destroy();\n} catch (reason) {\n  console.error(\"Load failed:\", reason?.name, reason?.message);\n}\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Worker URL resolution for bundlers (Vite/Webpack)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/webpack.js\n\nShows the recommended pattern for configuring PDF.js worker in bundlers like Vite or Webpack, using `new URL(..., import.meta.url)` to resolve the worker script path relative to the current module.\n\n```javascript\nconst pdfjs = require(\"./build/pdf.js\");\n\nif (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && \"Worker\" in window) {\n  pdfjs.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerPort = new Worker(\n    new URL(\"./build/pdf.worker.js\", import.meta.url)\n  );\n}\n\nmodule.exports = pdfjs;\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### GetDocumentParameters type alias (TypeScript)\n\nSource: https://github.com/mozilla/pdfjs-dist/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/getDocument.md\n\nType alias for the parameter accepted by getDocument. It can be a string, URL, TypedArray, ArrayBuffer, PDFDataRangeTransport, or DocumentInitParameters.\n\n```typescript\nexport type GetDocumentParameters =\n  | string | URL | TypedArray | ArrayBuffer\n  | PDFDataRangeTransport\n  | DocumentInitParameters;\n```"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"35c9b880-3fd0-48e7-b4d1-49eda1a9d9de","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Us