{"parentUuid":"856529fe-a512-4742-827f-6651578165c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpnCgc4DJbtnfedcd3vt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015DSRkC4JsXcDxdb7ZJCw2p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=\"C:/Users/jerem/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/2ea77955cf64b3d5/28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab/scratchpad\"; cat > \"$S/test-case.html\" <<'EOF'\n<html><body style=\"font-family:Georgia;font-size:12pt;margin:40px\">\n<h2>ALS Clinic — Case Summary (TEST DOCUMENT, synthetic)</h2>\n<p>Patient: A-0417. 58-year-old woman. Bulbar-onset ALS diagnosed 14 months ago (El Escorial: clinically probable).</p>\n<p>ALSFRS-R 38/48 (slope -0.9 points/month). FVC 72% predicted. Dysarthria, mild dysphagia.</p>\n<p>Genetics: ALS panel negative (SOD1, C9orf72, FUS, TARDBP).</p>\n<p>Medications: riluzole 50 mg BID; edaravone (oral); lisinopril 10 mg daily.</p>\n<p>Comorbidities: hypertension; CKD stage 2.</p>\n<div style=\"page-break-before:always\"></div>\n<h3>Social and preferences</h3>\n<p>Lives in Toronto, ON. OHIP plus private drug plan. Open to clinical trials; prefers outpatient care; would rather avoid daily injections.</p>\n<p>Referred for assessment of eligibility for MR-guided focused ultrasound blood-brain barrier opening.</p>\n</body></html>\nEOF\n\"/c/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe\" --headless=new --no-pdf-header-footer --user-data-dir=\"$S/chrome-prof2\" --print-to-pdf=\"$S/test-case.pdf\" \"file:///$S/test-case.html\" 2>/dev/null; ls -la \"$S/test-case.pdf\"","description":"Generate a synthetic two-page test case PDF","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":695336,"output_tokens":3079,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":201},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3079,"cache_read_input_tokens":695336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6547,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015DSRkC4JsXcDxdb7ZJCw2p":{"command":"S=\"C:/Users/jerem/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/2ea77955cf64b3d5/28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab/scratchpad\"; cat > \"$S/test-case.html\" <<'EOF'\n<html><body style=\"font-family:Georgia;font-size:12pt;margin:40px\">\n<h2>ALS Clinic — Case Summary (TEST DOCUMENT, synthetic)</h2>\n<p>Patient: A-0417. 58-year-old woman. Bulbar-onset ALS diagnosed 14 months ago (El Escorial: clinically probable).</p>\n<p>ALSFRS-R 38/48 (slope -0.9 points/month). FVC 72% predicted. Dysarthria, mild dysphagia.</p>\n<p>Genetics: ALS panel negative (SOD1, C9orf72, FUS, TARDBP).</p>\n<p>Medications: riluzole 50 mg BID; edaravone (oral); lisinopril 10 mg daily.</p>\n<p>Comorbidities: hypertension; CKD stage 2.</p>\n<div style=\"page-break-before:always\"></div>\n<h3>Social and preferences</h3>\n<p>Lives in Toronto, ON. OHIP plus private drug plan. Open to clinical trials; prefers outpatient care; would rather avoid daily injections.</p>\n<p>Referred for assessment of eligibility for MR-guided focused ultrasound blood-brain barrier opening.</p>\n</body></html>\nEOF\n\"/c/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe\" --headless=new --no-pdf-header-footer --user-data-dir=\"$S/chrome-prof2\" --print-to-pdf=\"$S/test-case.pdf\" \"file:///$S/test-case.html\" 2>/dev/null; ls -la \"$S/test-case.pdf\"","description":"Generate a synthetic two-page test case PDF","timeout":60000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3c6b29ea-24e3-419c-9f8f-f6c29c9f7bd