{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","id":"28df5d33-03ef-47f5-87c0-1442ff6e5e2d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:52:28.821Z","version":"2.1.319","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"5685418bd6f66308fa90ee5dade4a2397602d74a9bb9e15af07b03e1cb0aac0d","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"62fc7a6e-e64c-43fe-a1a9-3ee5693c7ea2","keep":635,"tail":["7bf7a3781efb1ab8193ab55e449a5953adb218877bb45115c79ce83fb1634254","8c8f7bcef89a3db9731427c2e4463fef66df8637e3bcb09474b67a1a5e053f61"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",636,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"98221b3b7c2c23ea6cea3a4fb9aa5f2c9d244fa9f26bc9d513400a1dca238e6e"}
{"parentUuid":"83446ae6-4902-4012-ac7c-e2fd98384bcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpnM7vXwTt3MTYzjFmzH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each step of the flow now has its own page, and the run starts from a patient-case PDF you upload. I tested the whole flow end to end in headless Chrome, with a synthetic two-page case PDF uploaded through the real file picker. The build passes.\n\n**Pipeline pages** (listed under \"Pipeline\" in the sidebar, each with a live status: pending, spinning while it runs, ticked when done):\n\n| | Page | What's on it |\n|---|---|---|\n| 00 | Patient case | Drop or choose the case PDF, preview its extracted text page by page, patient summary, research goal and ranking switches, \"Run 5 agents\" |\n| 01 | Patient analysis | Analysis agent's trace (it reads the PDF first), the patient card, then the written patient summary |\n| 02 | Profile agents | Five side-by-side columns, one per agent: hypothesis header, its own live trace, then its finished drug profile |\n| 03 | DRKG embedding | The embedding map, top matches per profile with cosine scores, and the embedding job's trace |\n| 04 | Research & ranking | Ranking table with live re-ranking switches, exclusions, and the research agent's trace |\n| 05 | Report | The cited report with \"Save as PDF\"; it now also names which case file it came from |\n\nDuring a run the app moves to each page as its stage starts, so a judge can just watch. If you click anywhere yourself, it stops following. \"Skip to results\" works from any page, and the run keeps going while you look around.\n\n**Case PDF**\n- **Reading:** text is extracted in the browser with pdf.js, so the patient's file is never uploaded. That seemed the right default for patient data.\n- **What the agent sees:** in the analysis trace, the first step is `pdf.extract_text` on your file, followed by the word count and an excerpt of what was read.\n- **Scanned PDFs:** image-only PDFs have no extractable text, and the preview says so. They'd need OCR.\n\n**One limitation to be upfront about:** the run is still scripted. Uploading a PDF changes what the analysis trace shows, but the structured patient profile and everything after it still use the built-in sample patient (A-0417). The case page says this on screen. Making the agents actually read the PDF needs the real backend. The extracted text is already passed into the run function (`runDemoPipeline` in `src/lib/pipeline.ts`), so a backend can take it from there.\n\n**Code changes**\n- **Shared run state:** moved to `src/lib/run-store.tsx`, so every page reads the same run.\n- **Pages:** in `src/components/discovery/pages.tsx`, with shared pieces in `pieces.tsx` and PDF reading in `src/lib/case-pdf.ts`.\n- **Removed:** the old single-page workspace, and the Genetics, Medications, Clinic visits and Symptom diary placeholders. The case PDF covers that information now.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":714636,"output_tokens":969,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":714636,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8d5ed298-7027-4b86-b984-7bfeda986497","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpnM7bSroAiSMHcLUhM7","requestRef":"28df5d33-03ef-47f5-87c0-1442ff6e5e2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"72710fe0-0f05-4069-897c-20c765daa765","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:52:38.903Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
