{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","hash":"2fa56b6f59c04db3dc21f56265f5b7f8f7dc82f35debad9fc6a0f2bc99238a29","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I read your two asks as:\n1. **Remove the five-stage progress strip** under each page heading. The sidebar already shows each step's status.\n2. **Run the pipeline one stage at a time.** After each stage finishes, the run pauses until you click to start the next. The automatic page-following goes away too.\n\nStarting with splitting the scripted run so each stage can run on its own:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V5eS624viHGZgrH7Xi2veA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026/frontend && grep -n \"export function runDemoPipeline\" -A 25 src/lib/pipeline.ts","description":"View current runner"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
