{"parentUuid":"1db36127-20e4-4f8c-b466-d40286d7cacd","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"We're building the Addo Labs ALS drug-discovery site. The pipeline now advances one step per click, the progress strip is gone and the background is React Bits Gradient ASCII. Next, try it with `npm run dev`, then commit.","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:26:53.507Z","uuid":"d173fa0e-3f89-439f-aadb-a1c8b639c904","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"d173fa0e-3f89-439f-aadb-a1c8b639c904","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49e38bf9-70c2-46f3-9a2e-7c8492331aa8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"For the landing page, I want the neuron to be horizantal around the top part of the page. Move the name to the bottom left area and have it so that the glow from the synapse propagates across the entire screen to the axon terminals and eventually to the name"},"uuid":"b8a9a654-21a9-4cc2-95e1-90ecd02dbd7d","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:55:20.578Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":24,"turnIndex":35},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"b8a9a654-21a9-4cc2-95e1-90ecd02dbd7d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t@AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t# Claude-specific notes\n6\t\n7\tEverything about the project and how we work is in `AGENTS.md`, imported\n8\tabove — including the session ritual (read `docs/STATUS.md`, update it before\n9\tyou stop). This file only covers what's specific to working here as Claude.\n10\t\n11\t## Skills\n12\t\n13\t21 skills under `.claude/skills/`, installed via `npx skills` and pinned in\n14\t`skills-lock.json` so the whole team gets the identical set. Audited on\n15\tinstall: none declare hooks, the only bundled script is a Tailwind docs sync.\n16\t\n17\t**Load them rather than improvising — that's the point of having them.**\n18\t\n19\t### Before writing any UI\n20\t\n21\t- `baseline-ui` — ~40 MUST/NEVER Tailwind rules. Run as a linter pass.\n22\t- `emil-design-eng` — the motion decision framework. Durations by element\n23\t  type, stagger 30–80ms, custom easing curves, never `ease-in` on UI.\n24\t- `better-ui` — exact radius/shadow/press values.\n25\t- `better-typography` — `tabular-nums` on every readout, line-height\n26\t  1.1 / 1.2–1.3 / 1.5, −0.01em tracking above 24px.\n27\t- `better-colors` — semantic tokens, OKLCH ramps, and the rule that matters\n28\t  most here: colour must never be the only carrier of pass/fail.\n29\t- `apple-design` — spring feel, reduced-motion, material and depth.\n30\t\n31\t### Animation\n32\t\n33\t`animate` to build · `review-animations` to critique a diff ·\n34\t`improve-animations` to audit the whole app · `find-animation-opportunities`\n35\tto find what should move · `fixing-motion-performance` for jank ·\n36\t`vercel-react-view-transitions` for the View Transition API.\n37\t\n38\tThere is **no trustworthy Motion/Framer Motion skill** — the best candidate\n39\tgives blanket `will-change` advice. Rely on the above.\n40\t\n41\t### Tailwind and React\n42\t\n43\t- `tailwind-4-docs` — **check before writing config or `@theme`.** v4 differs\n44\t  sharply from the v3 that dominates training data.\n45\t- `tailwind-v4-shadcn` — the Vite + Tailwind v4 setup and its CSS-variable\n46\t  gotchas. `frontend/` uses exactly this stack, shadcn half included.\n47\t- `tailwind-design-system` — tokens and component structure.\n48\t- `vercel-react-best-practices` — perf review before the demo.\n49\t\n50\t### Review\n51\t\n52\t- `better-interface` — orchestrates `better-ui` / `-typography` / `-colors` /\n53\t  `-accessibility` into one ranked report. **This is the single pre-demo pass.**\n54\t- `better-accessibility` — WCAG 2.2 with severity.\n55\t- `prototype` — divergent layout variants on one route with a switcher, for\n56\t  settling a shape fast instead of iterating in place.\n57\t- `web-design-guidelines` — rules vendored to `guidelines.md`, so it works\n58\t  offline at the expo.\n59\t\n60\t### Not installed, deliberately\n61\t\n62\t`taste-skill@design-taste-frontend` (installs a Stop hook, runs headless\n63\tChrome, failed a third-party trust audit) · `ui-ux-pro-max` and `ui-taste`\n64\t(lookup databases and paid-MCP routers, no judgment) · `gsap-skills` (adds a\n65\tdependency, silent on exit animation) · `knowledge-work-plugins@data-visualization`\n66\t(matplotlib, not React).\n67\t\n68\tOne-off slop check needing no install: `npx impeccable detect frontend/src/`\n69\t— 62 deterministic rules, no LLM.\n70\t\n71\tMaintenance: `npx skills update` · `npx skills add owner/repo@skill -y`.\n72\t\n73\t## shadcn/ui in `frontend/`\n74\t\n75\tComponents live in `frontend/src/components/ui/`. Add more with\n76\t`npx shadcn@latest add <name>` — but the CLI resolves `@` as a literal\n77\tdirectory here and writes `cn` imports as `from \"cn\"`, so after adding, move\n78\t`frontend/@/components/ui/*` into `src/components/ui/` and fix that import.\n79\tThe hand-written `components.json` is correct; don't run `init` over it.\n80\t\n81\t## Also available from Henri's global plugins\n82\t\n83\t`frontend-design` and `dataviz` are enabled on his account, not in this repo —\n84\tteammates cloning this won't have them. Don't rely on them for anything a\n85\tcommitted skill should cover.","rereadEntry":{"timestamp":1794113550520,"contentHash":"sijls50l3z64","contentLength":3670}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a66c2273-ea0b-4d57-a480-4158526690e9","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:55:20.578Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\CLAUDE.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t@AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t# Claude-specific notes\n6\t\n7\tEverything about the project and how we work is in `AGENTS.md`, imported\n8\tabove — including the session ritual (read `docs/STATUS.md`, update it before\n9\tyou stop). This file only covers what's specific to working here as Claude.\n10\t\n11\t## Skills\n12\t\n13\t21 skills under `.claude/skills/`, installed via `npx skills` and pinned in\n14\t`skills-lock.json` so the whole team gets the identical set. Audited on\n15\tinstall: none declare hooks, the only bundled script is a Tailwind docs sync.\n16\t\n17\t**Load them rather than improvising — that's the point of having them.**\n18\t\n19\t### Before writing any UI\n20\t\n21\t- `baseline-ui` — ~40 MUST/NEVER Tailwind rules. Run as a linter pass.\n22\t- `emil-design-eng` — the motion decision framework. Durations by element\n23\t  type, stagger 30–80ms, custom easing curves, never `ease-in` on UI.\n24\t- `better-ui` — exact radius/shadow/press values.\n25\t- `better-typography` — `tabular-nums` on every readout, line-height\n26\t  1.1 / 1.2–1.3 / 1.5, −0.01em tracking above 24px.\n27\t- `better-colors` — semantic tokens, OKLCH ramps, and the rule that matters\n28\t  most here: colour must never be the only carrier of pass/fail.\n29\t- `apple-design` — spring feel, reduced-motion, material and depth.\n30\t\n31\t### Animation\n32\t\n33\t`animate` to build · `review-animations` to critique a diff ·\n34\t`improve-animations` to audit the whole app · `find-animation-opportunities`\n35\tto find what should move · `fixing-motion-performance` for jank ·\n36\t`vercel-react-view-transitions` for the View Transition API.\n37\t\n38\tThere is **no trustworthy Motion/Framer Motion skill** — the best candidate\n39\tgives blanket `will-change` advice. Rely on the above.\n40\t\n41\t### Tailwind and React\n42\t\n43\t- `tailwind-4-docs` — **check before writing config or `@theme`.** v4 differs\n44\t  sharply from the v3 that dominates training data.\n45\t- `tailwind-v4-shadcn` — the Vite + Tailwind v4 setup and its CSS-variable\n46\t  gotchas. `frontend/` uses exactly this stack, shadcn half included.\n47\t- `tailwind-design-system` — tokens and component structure.\n48\t- `vercel-react-best-practices` — perf review before the demo.\n49\t\n50\t### Review\n51\t\n52\t- `better-interface` — orchestrates `better-ui` / `-typography` / `-colors` /\n53\t  `-accessibility` into one ranked report. **This is the single pre-demo pass.**\n54\t- `better-accessibility` — WCAG 2.2 with severity.\n55\t- `prototype` — divergent layout variants on one route with a switcher, for\n56\t  settling a shape fast instead of iterating in place.\n57\t- `web-design-guidelines` — rules vendored to `guidelines.md`, so it works\n58\t  offline at the expo.\n59\t\n60\t### Not installed, deliberately\n61\t\n62\t`taste-skill@design-taste-frontend` (installs a Stop hook, runs headless\n63\tChrome, failed a third-party trust audit) · `ui-ux-pro-max` and `ui-taste`\n64\t(lookup databases and paid-MCP routers, no judgment) · `gsap-skills` (adds a\n65\tdependency, silent on exit animation) · `knowledge-work-plugins@data-visualization`\n66\t(matplotlib, not React).\n67\t\n68\tOne-off slop check needing no install: `npx impeccable detect frontend/src/`\n69\t— 62 deterministic rules, no LLM.\n70\t\n71\tMaintenance: `npx skills update` · `npx skills add owner/repo@skill -y`.\n72\t\n73\t## shadcn/ui in `frontend/`\n74\t\n75\tComponents live in `frontend/src/components/ui/`. Add more with\n76\t`npx shadcn@latest add <name>` — but the CLI resolves `@` as a literal\n77\tdirectory here and writes `cn` imports as `from \"cn\"`, so after adding, move\n78\t`frontend/@/components/ui/*` into `src/components/ui/` and fix that import.\n79\tThe hand-written `components.json` is correct; don't run `init` over it.\n80\t\n81\t## Also available from Henri's global plugins\n82\t\n83\t`frontend-design` and `dataviz` are enabled on his account, not in this repo —\n84\tteammates cloning this won't have them. Don't rely on them for anything a\n85\tcommitted skill should cover.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026\\frontend","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
