g_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.492.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.492.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.498.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.500.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.506.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.510.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.512.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.512.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.514.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.518.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.518.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.524.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.526.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.529.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.529.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1341,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Kds22MUgMAZBM4yPpeubHF":{"command":"cd /c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026 && git status --short | head -30; git log --oneline -5; ls; cat AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null | head -120; echo ===; cat docs/STATUS.md 2>/dev/null | head -80","description":"Check repo state, AGENTS.md and STATUS.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ec069d29-ec2b-4d86-a7fe-98595399d046","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgps9GCcVYu1w5QW7M1u7","requestRef":"4eaacacd-6d72-4885-867e-0f0e128327a0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b54a8d38-c477-4cfa-8757-f76e6d5656e1","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:55:33.871Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jerem\\BioHacks-2026","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"frontend/diagnosis"}
{"parentUuid":"b54a8d38-c477-4cfa-8757-f76e6d5656e1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49e38bf9-70c2-46f3-9a2e-7c8492331aa8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kds22MUgMAZBM4yPpeubHF","type":"tool_result","content":"0254c6c Merge pull request #3 from penguinyogurt/frontend/diagnosis\nb896229 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into frontend/diagnosis\n759be20 Tell Jeremy how to clear the tsbuildinfo conflict I caused\n64e5ffc frontend updates\n0ca9d6a Give the claim protocol a threshold and a path for new work\nAGENTS.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncontract\ndata\ndocs\nfrontend\nREADME.md\nskills-lock.json\n# BioHacks 2026 — repo guide for humans and AI\n\n**This file is the single source of truth.** `CLAUDE.md` imports it; Codex,\nCursor and Copilot read it directly. If you change how the project works,\nchange it **here**, not in a second file and not in a DM.\n\nDevpost closes **Sun 2026-11-08 11:30 am**; expo judging 1:30–3:00 pm. Treat\n**9:00 am Sunday** as the real deadline and leave the last two hours for the\npitch.\n\n---\n\n## Read this before you touch anything\n\nFour people are working in parallel with AI agents. The thing that has cost\nus the most time is not bugs — it is **two people building the same thing\nbecause neither knew what the other was doing.** We have already shipped\nthree separate frontends for one project.\n\nSo, in order, every session:\n\n1. **Read [`docs/STATUS.md`](docs/STATUS.md).** It is the shared task board:\n   what is claimed, what is open, what is done. Fifteen seconds.\n2. **Claim before you write code** — put your name on the line, commit\n   *just that file*, push immediately. Not on the board yet? Add it and\n   claim it in the same push. A claim that lands after your work is\n   worthless. Small stuff is exempt; the board says where the line is.\n3. **Check the map below** for which directory your work belongs in. If your\n   change doesn't obviously fit one, say so before writing code.\n4. **Before you stop, update the board.** Move your line to Done, or back to\n   Open with one line on where you left it. Even \"I got nowhere on X\" is\n   worth more to the other three than silence.\n\n**If you are an agent, steps 1, 2 and 4 are not optional and you do them\nwithout being asked.** You are one of several agents working this repo at\nthe same time, driven by different people on different harnesses, and you\ncannot see the others. The board is the only thing that stops two of you\nwriting the same file from opposite directions. If a task you were about to\nstart is already claimed by someone else, stop and tell your human rather\nthan doing it anyway.\n\n---\n\n## What's here\n\n| Directory | What it is | Stack |\n|---|---|---|\n| `frontend/` | **Motus** — the product. Longitudinal at-home ALS monitoring: speech, typing and handwriting tracked against a personal baseline. Landing + dashboard. | Vite · React 19 · TS · Tailwind v4 · shadcn/ui · Supabase · three |\n| `contract/` | The `data/pipeline.json` schema, its tests, and the CLI validator. Owned by nobody, depended on by everybody. | zod · node:test |\n| `data/` | `pipeline.json` — the frozen contract plus a hand-written sample. | — |\n| `docs/` | Specs, research, decisions, status. **See \"Documentation\" below.** | — |\n| `.claude/skills/` | 21 pinned design/frontend skills. See `CLAUDE.md`. | — |\n| `.workspace/` | Your personal scratch, gitignored. See its README. | — |\n\n### Work that lives on branches, not on main\n\nNot everything is merged. Before starting something, check whether it already\nexists here:\n\n| Branch | What's on it |\n|---|---|\n| `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | The **drug-repurposing pipeline** — `bbb_model.py`, `patient_filter.py`, `merge.py`, `graveyard.py`, scored across 3,791 compounds. This is live work, not abandoned. |\n| `cursor/facial-als-validation` | **FaceCheck** (`facecheck/`) — MediaPipe facial-amplitude prototype. Spec: [`docs/FACECHECK_SPEC.md`](docs/FACECHECK_SPEC.md). |\n| `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech and diagnostic test apps (`master-app/`, `speech-test-good/`, `facial-test/`, `line-test/`). **Unrelated git history** — it does not share a root with `main`. Merging it is a decision, not a chore; log it in `docs/DECISIONS.md` first. |\n\n**Nothing above is dead.** If you think a track should be dropped, that is a\ndecision — write it down, don't silently stop maintaining it.\n\n---\n\n## The rules that keep four people from colliding\n\n### One track per branch, one owner per file\n\nTwo agents editing the same file in parallel is how we lose an afternoon.\nClaim your area in `docs/STATUS.md` and stay in it. If you need a change in\nsomebody else's file, say so in STATUS rather than reaching in.\n\n### Don't build a second one\n\nBefore creating a new app, page, module or script: **search for it first.**\n`git branch -r`, then grep. Three frontends happened because nobody looked.\nIf what exists is wrong, fix or replace it deliberately and say so — don't\nleave both standing.\n\n### Integration happens through files, not imports\n\nEach module writes **one JSON file**. Nobody imports anybody else's code.\n\n```\nthe Python pipeline  → data/pipeline.json   (validated by contract/)\nFaceCheck            → facecheck.session.v3 (its own export)\nfrontend/            → reads what it's given, imports no pipeline code\n```\n\nThis decoupling is the schedule: all four tracks can be built at once and a\nbroken module doesn't block the rest. **Do not propose refactors that couple\nthem.**\n\n### The contract is frozen\n\n`data/pipeline.json`'s executable definition is\n[`contract/contract.ts`](contract/contract.ts); the annotated prose version is\n[`docs/CONTRACT.md`](docs/CONTRACT.md).\n\nCheck your output without running any frontend:\n\n```bash\nnpm run validate --prefix contract -- path/to/your.json\n```\n\nExits non-zero with readable problems. If the shape genuinely must change:\nupdate `contract/contract.ts`, update the sample in `data/pipeline.json`, run\n`npm test --prefix contract`, log it in `docs/DECISIONS.md`, and **tell the\nteam in the same breath.**\n\n---\n\n## Documentation — what goes in `docs/`\n\n===\n# Status — the shared task board\n\n**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every\nsession. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.\n\nThere is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and\nfour people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in\ncommon, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below\nis what makes it work.\n\nLast updated: **2026-11-07**\n\n---\n\n## How to claim (all of it)\n\n1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.\n2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim\n   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.\n   ```bash\n   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push\n   ```\n3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.\n   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.\n4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or\n   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked\n   silently is the same as a task nobody did.\n\nIf two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one\nmarkdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.\n\n**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it\nin the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.\n\n**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.\nSkip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same\ntime: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything\nunder ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a\nshared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.\nA board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.\n\n---\n\n## In flight — claimed, don't touch\n\n| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |\n| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |\n| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |\n| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |\n| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |\n| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |\n\n> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.\n\n## Open — unclaimed, grab one\n\nOrdered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.\n\n| Track | Task | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |\n| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |\n| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |\n| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |\n| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |\n| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |\n| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |\n| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |\n| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |\n\n## Done\n\n- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract\n  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),\n  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.\n- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.\n- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged\n  (PRs #1, #2).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"75a4ae1f-6184-4dce-8d1a-12726a07518e","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:55:35.912Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"0254c6c Merge pull request #3 from penguinyogurt/frontend/diagnosis\nb896229 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into frontend/diagnosis\n759be20 Tell Jeremy how to clear the tsbuildinfo conflict I caused\n64e5ffc frontend updates\n0ca9d6a Give the claim protocol a threshold and a path for new work\nAGENTS.md\nCLAUDE.md\ncontract\ndata\ndocs\nfrontend\nREADME.md\nskills-lock.json\n# BioHacks 2026 — repo guide for humans and AI\n\n**This file is the single source of truth.** `CLAUDE.md` imports it; Codex,\nCursor and Copilot read it directly. If you change how the project works,\nchange it **here**, not in a second file and not in a DM.\n\nDevpost closes **Sun 2026-11-08 11:30 am**; expo judging 1:30–3:00 pm. Treat\n**9:00 am Sunday** as the real deadline and leave the last two hours for the\npitch.\n\n---\n\n## Read this before you touch anything\n\nFour people are working in parallel with AI agents. The thing that has cost\nus the most time is not bugs — it is **two people building the same thing\nbecause neither knew what the other was doing.** We have already shipped\nthree separate frontends for one project.\n\nSo, in order, every session:\n\n1. **Read [`docs/STATUS.md`](docs/STATUS.md).** It is the shared task board:\n   what is claimed, what is open, what is done. Fifteen seconds.\n2. **Claim before you write code** — put your name on the line, commit\n   *just that file*, push immediately. Not on the board yet? Add it and\n   claim it in the same push. A claim that lands after your work is\n   worthless. Small stuff is exempt; the board says where the line is.\n3. **Check the map below** for which directory your work belongs in. If your\n   change doesn't obviously fit one, say so before writing code.\n4. **Before you stop, update the board.** Move your line to Done, or back to\n   Open with one line on where you left it. Even \"I got nowhere on X\" is\n   worth more to the other three than silence.\n\n**If you are an agent, steps 1, 2 and 4 are not optional and you do them\nwithout being asked.** You are one of several agents working this repo at\nthe same time, driven by different people on different harnesses, and you\ncannot see the others. The board is the only thing that stops two of you\nwriting the same file from opposite directions. If a task you were about to\nstart is already claimed by someone else, stop and tell your human rather\nthan doing it anyway.\n\n---\n\n## What's here\n\n| Directory | What it is | Stack |\n|---|---|---|\n| `frontend/` | **Motus** — the product. Longitudinal at-home ALS monitoring: speech, typing and handwriting tracked against a personal baseline. Landing + dashboard. | Vite · React 19 · TS · Tailwind v4 · shadcn/ui · Supabase · three |\n| `contract/` | The `data/pipeline.json` schema, its tests, and the CLI validator. Owned by nobody, depended on by everybody. | zod · node:test |\n| `data/` | `pipeline.json` — the frozen contract plus a hand-written sample. | — |\n| `docs/` | Specs, research, decisions, status. **See \"Documentation\" below.** | — |\n| `.claude/skills/` | 21 pinned design/frontend skills. See `CLAUDE.md`. | — |\n| `.workspace/` | Your personal scratch, gitignored. See its README. | — |\n\n### Work that lives on branches, not on main\n\nNot everything is merged. Before starting something, check whether it already\nexists here:\n\n| Branch | What's on it |\n|---|---|\n| `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | The **drug-repurposing pipeline** — `bbb_model.py`, `patient_filter.py`, `merge.py`, `graveyard.py`, scored across 3,791 compounds. This is live work, not abandoned. |\n| `cursor/facial-als-validation` | **FaceCheck** (`facecheck/`) — MediaPipe facial-amplitude prototype. Spec: [`docs/FACECHECK_SPEC.md`](docs/FACECHECK_SPEC.md). |\n| `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech and diagnostic test apps (`master-app/`, `speech-test-good/`, `facial-test/`, `line-test/`). **Unrelated git history** — it does not share a root with `main`. Merging it is a decision, not a chore; log it in `docs/DECISIONS.md` first. |\n\n**Nothing above is dead.** If you think a track should be dropped, that is a\ndecision — write it down, don't silently stop maintaining it.\n\n---\n\n## The rules that keep four people from colliding\n\n### One track per branch, one owner per file\n\nTwo agents editing the same file in parallel is how we lose an afternoon.\nClaim your area in `docs/STATUS.md` and stay in it. If you need a change in\nsomebody else's file, say so in STATUS rather than reaching in.\n\n### Don't build a second one\n\nBefore creating a new app, page, module or script: **search for it first.**\n`git branch -r`, then grep. Three frontends happened because nobody looked.\nIf what exists is wrong, fix or replace it deliberately and say so — don't\nleave both standing.\n\n### Integration happens through files, not imports\n\nEach module writes **one JSON file**. Nobody imports anybody else's code.\n\n```\nthe Python pipeline  → data/pipeline.json   (validated by contract/)\nFaceCheck            → facecheck.session.v3 (its own export)\nfrontend/            → reads what it's given, imports no pipeline code\n```\n\nThis decoupling is the schedule: all four tracks can be built at once and a\nbroken module doesn't block the rest. **Do not propose refactors that couple\nthem.**\n\n### The contract is frozen\n\n`data/pipeline.json`'s executable definition is\n[`contract/contract.ts`](contract/contract.ts); the annotated prose version is\n[`docs/CONTRACT.md`](docs/CONTRACT.md).\n\nCheck your output without running any frontend:\n\n```bash\nnpm run validate --prefix contract -- path/to/your.json\n```\n\nExits non-zero with readable problems. If the shape genuinely must change:\nupdate `contract/contract.ts`, update the sample in `data/pipeline.json`, run\n`npm test --prefix contract`, log it in `docs/DECISIONS.md`, and **tell the\nteam in the same breath.**\n\n---\n\n## Documentation — what goes in `docs/`\n\n===\n# Status — the shared task board\n\n**This is the one place work is claimed.** Read it at the start of every\nsession. Claim before you write code. Release when you stop.\n\nThere is no task framework to install — `gh` isn't on these machines and\nfour people on three different AI harnesses have exactly one medium in\ncommon, which is this repo. So the board is a file, and the protocol below\nis what makes it work.\n\nLast updated: **2026-11-07**\n\n---\n\n## How to claim (all of it)\n\n1. **`git pull`** — then put your name on the line you want, in **In flight**.\n2. **Commit just this file and push immediately.** Don't bundle the claim\n   with your work; the claim is worthless if it lands an hour later.\n   ```bash\n   git pull && git add docs/STATUS.md && git commit -m \"claim: <task>\" && git push\n   ```\n3. **If the push is rejected**, someone claimed something while you typed.\n   `git pull --rebase`, check your task is still free, push again.\n4. **When you stop** — done, blocked, or bored — move the line to **Done** or\n   back to **Open**, with one line on where you left it. A task parked\n   silently is the same as a task nobody did.\n\nIf two of you end up on the same line anyway, that's a conflict in one\nmarkdown row. Keep both names, talk, move on.\n\n**Your task isn't on the board?** Most won't be. Add the line and claim it\nin the same push — that *is* the claim. Don't go looking for permission.\n\n**When not to claim.** Claiming costs a push, so it has to buy something.\nSkip it for anything another person could not plausibly start at the same\ntime: reading code, answering a question, a typo, a one-line fix, anything\nunder ~10 minutes. Claim when you're about to **create a file, change a\nshared one, or work somewhere for a while** — that's when collisions happen.\nA board full of \"fixed a typo\" is a board nobody reads.\n\n---\n\n## In flight — claimed, don't touch\n\n| Who | Track | Branch | Task | Blocked on |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Jeremy | discovery | `main` | FUS discovery pipeline — scripted end to end. See `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` | A live backend behind `runDemoPipeline` |\n| Jeremy | frontend | `main` | Motus dashboard — overview landed, 15 views still placeholders | Supabase keys |\n| Neo | pipeline | `cursor/pipeline-graph-ui` | Drug pipeline — BBB + patient filter scored over 3,791 compounds | — |\n| Neo | facecheck | `cursor/facial-als-validation` | FaceCheck MediaPipe prototype | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §2 gaps |\n| Levi | speech | `Master-UI-Neo-Face-Integration` | Speech + diagnostic test apps | No spec in `docs/` yet |\n| Henri | repo | `main` | Cleanup, specs, this board | — |\n\n> Names are from git history. Fix them if they're wrong.\n\n## Open — unclaimed, grab one\n\nOrdered roughly by what hurts most if it's still open on Sunday morning.\n\n| Track | Task | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| **decision** | **Pick the product: discovery pipeline or Motus.** Both ship on `main`, in one sidebar, sharing nothing else | 90 seconds, one argument. Everything below depends on this |\n| **decision** | **Pick the name.** Code says *Addo Labs*, landing page says *motus* | A judge sees both in one scroll |\n| discovery | Wire the graveyard's `never_arrived` bucket in as the FUS candidate pool | It already exists in `data/pipeline.json` and is exactly the right set — `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` §1 |\n| discovery | Real citations for the Sunnybrook MRgFUS claim; be precise about human vs proposed | The whole pitch rests on it, and someone will ask |\n| pipeline | Port the Python onto a branch cut from `main` (leave `data/*.json` and `artifacts/` behind) | `main` has no pipeline code today |\n| speech | Write `docs/SPEECH_SPEC.md` | The only track with no spec — nobody else can pick it up |\n| frontend | Decide demo mode: signed-in or sample data | Sample works today with no keys |\n| facecheck | Decide: own page, or a tab in the app | `FACECHECK_SPEC.md` §7 |\n| discovery | A real backend behind `runDemoPipeline` — stretch | The seam is clean; don't collapse it under time pressure |\n\n## Done\n\n- **2026-11-07** · Henri · Repo cleanup: `app/` and `web/` deleted, contract\n  extracted to `contract/`, `.gitignore` rewritten (`.env` was exposed),\n  `.workspace/` added, CI deleted — run `npm test --prefix contract` yourself.\n- **2026-11-07** · Henri · `DISCOVERY_SPEC.md` written from Jeremy's pitch.\n- **2026-11-07** · Jeremy · Discovery pipeline UI + Motus dashboard merged\n  (PRs #1, #2).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ec069d29-ec2b-4d86-a7fe-98595399d046","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026/frontend","root":"/c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026","branch":"frontend/diagnosis","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"penguinyogurt/BioHacks-2026","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"penguinyogurt/BioHacks-2026","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"gi