{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"28437234-f1be-440d-9452-c51de1bd38ab","hash":"649abf8f66b94a7cc53997c4c1f75b666985e6f74d95f03337549969233b6199","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The orange trail now only appears between the terminals and the name, and I've made the layout change: the neuron sits lower and further left, slightly smaller and tilted toward the text, and the text block is moved in from the right edge.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LpZbt8UoKAy7HTEACcPqL5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/jerem/BioHacks-2026/frontend && python - <<'PYEOF'\np='src/components/neuron-viewer.tsx'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\ndef r(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nr(\"\"\"const FILL_W = 0.9 // share of the page width the cell spans, soma to terminals\nconst MAX_CROSS = 0.74 // cap on the dendrite spread, as a share of page height\nconst AXIS_Y = 0.34 // where the axon lies, from the top of the page\n\"\"\",\"\"\"const FILL_W = 0.8 // share of the page width the cell spans, soma to terminals\nconst MAX_CROSS = 0.7 // cap on the dendrite spread, as a share of page height\nconst AXIS_Y = 0.42 // where the cell's centre sits, from the top of the page\nconst SHIFT_X = -0.06 // nudge left, as a share of page width\nconst TILT_DEG = -8 // slight downward slope toward the terminals (and the name)\n\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"  const lift = viewport.height * (0.5 - AXIS_Y)\"\"\",\"\"\"  const lift = viewport.height * (0.5 - AXIS_Y)\n  const shift = viewport.width * SHIFT_X\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"    <group position={[0, lift, 0]}>\"\"\",\"\"\"    // Tilted frame: the roll happens inside it, so the cell still turns about its own length.\n    <group position={[shift, lift, 0]} rotation={[0, 0, (TILT_DEG * Math.PI) / 180]}>\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\np='src/pages/Landing.tsx'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf8').read()\na='<main 